# Roguelike RPG

Read `@.cursor/config.json` for stack and path defaults. Treat `docs/game_design.md` as the source of truth for mechanics.

## Stack

- Local Node app with Three.js. Prefer npm. Do not add Next, Nuxt, or other app frameworks unless asked.
- Keep the first playable loop small: run locally, reload in the browser, no backend unless the design requires it.
- Prefer plain JavaScript until the design doc says otherwise.

## Layout

- Design docs live under `docs/`.
- Application source will live under `src/` once the Node app is initialized.
- Do not invent folder conventions beyond what the current repo already uses.

## Working style

- Capture mechanics in the design doc before implementing them.
- Do not commit `.env` files, credentials, or generated `dist/` / `node_modules/`.
- Do not create git commits or push unless Josh asks.
